{%- comment -%}
  DOFEK's style layer.

  The sheets sit on top of `pluma.css` rather than replacing it: the two
  Hebrew faces and the wrapper are already right, and rebuilding them would
  only risk getting them wrong. They load after it so their posture wins,
  and `wf-tokens.css` restates the palette, which is the one file to open to
  change a colour. It is the file that makes this shop black and white.

  `pdp.css` and `pl-story.css` are gone. The product page here is `wf-product`,
  which carries its own rules in these sheets, so neither has anything left
  to style and both were pure weight on the heaviest page in the shop.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'overflow-list.css' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'style' }}
{{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

{%- comment -%}
  Rubik for headlines, Assistant for text. Both are drawn for Hebrew, so the
  page never falls back to a Latin face with patched Hebrew glyphs. Fetched as
  print and promoted on load, so a slow font server cannot hold up first paint.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pl_fonts = 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Assistant:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Rubik:wght@500;600;700&display=swap' -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="style" href="{{ pl_fonts }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pl_fonts }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'; this.onload=null;">
<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pl_fonts }}"></noscript>

{{ 'pluma.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  wf.css is three files. The division is a transport limit rather than a
  design one, and wf-tokens.css carries the reason. Order matters only in
  that the tokens come first; nothing in wf-shop.css is overridden by wf.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'wf-tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'wf.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'wf-shop.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  The guarantee, in its own sheet. It is the one block of rules that states a
  commercial promise rather than a layout, the merchant will edit it when the
  promise changes, and a named 5KB file is where they will find it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'wf-vow.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  The phone's corrections to the inherited components, on every template.
  It is last of the shared sheets because it overrides them, and it is tiny
  because it is a list of eleven type sizes and one tap target, not a
  parallel design.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'df-mobile.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  The home page, in its own 12KB sheet. It is the only template that uses any
  of it, and it is also the one template that has to paint before a visitor
  decides whether this shop is worth a second screen, so it is requested
  there and nowhere else.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
  {{ 'df.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  DOFEK's own product page, which is its own template and shares nothing
  with the one below but the palette. Two sheets: the buying block, and
  everything under it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.suffix == 'dofek-knee' -%}
  {{ 'df-pdp.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'df-long.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The long product page carries about 10KB of rules nothing else uses: the
  before and after pair, the numbered rails, the comparison table and the
  questions. Shipping that on the homepage and the collection pages would be
  pure weight on the two templates that decide whether a visitor stays at
  all, so it is requested on the product template and nowhere else.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.name == 'product' and template.suffix != 'dofek-knee' -%}
  {{ 'wf-pdp.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'wf-pdp-long.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'wf-pdp2.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}

<script src="{{ 'pluma.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
